+
+## Schema 3: API access and audit
+
+`apiKeys` contains `{ key, name, role }` records; roles are `viewer`, `cook`,
+and `manager`. `audit` is an append-only array of HTTP data-write records
+`{ time, name, method, path, status }`. Keys themselves never appear in audit.
+Schema 2 migrates by adding empty arrays, preserving existing values if present.
+Older files require keys to be configured before API access is possible.
+The seed contains one example key per role.
